 "pdf": "ads7142.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3 (pins), p.4 (ROC: AVDD, DVDD 1.65-3.6 V; digital inputs to DVDD + 0.3 V), p.6 (manual-mode tconv 1.8 us), p.7 (autonomous tconv/tcycle), p.9 (tVD-DAT 0.9 us fast mode), p.22 (straight binary, Table 1), p.23 (Table 2 address resistors), p.23-24 (data buffer), p.27 (general call, HS mode), p.28-30 (opcodes, register read/write frames), p.31-34 (power-up, manual mode, Figure 56), p.34-41 (autonomous / high-precision modes), p.43-59 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs and the input configurations (CHANNEL_INPUT_CFG: two single-ended, remote-ground, pseudo-differential); every conversion returns the 0 V code 000h; AVDD is the reference",
  "I2C address resistors on ADDR (Table 2): only the two tie cases are modeled, ADDR to GND (R2 0 ohm, also both open) 18h and ADDR to AVDD (R1 0 ohm) 1Fh; the 11k/33k/100k choices 19h-1Eh and the address re-evaluation general call (00h then 04h) are not",
  "the read frame is always manual-mode data (12-bit result then 0000b); the autonomous-mode 16-word data buffer FIFO (DATA_BUFFER_OPMODE start/stop burst, pre/post alert), DOUT_FORMAT channel ID / DATA_VALID bits, and high-precision-mode accumulator results (ACC_EN, ACC_CHx registers stay 0) are not modeled",
  "a register read (opcode 10h/30h) answers only the next read frame (protocol 'next'); continuous-block read/write (30h/28h) move only the first register; set bit (18h) is a plain write and clear bit (20h) is ignored",
  "DEVICE_RESET works without the WKEY = 1010b unlock and resets WKEY and the latched alert flags too (the datasheet keeps them); DEV_RST, TRIG_OFFCAL, SEQ_START and SEQ_ABORT read back as written (datasheet: write-only); nCLK values below 21/18 are not clamped",
  "manual-mode conversions: one per read frame (tconv 1.8 us max); clock stretching, the continuous-SCL conversion stream and the 140 kSPS throughput limit are not timed; autonomous cycle time (nCLK x tHSO/tLPO, OSC_SEL) and the channel sequencer (AUTO_SEQ_CHEN) are not modeled: SEL_OPMODE = 110b converts continuously at 1.8 us",
  "BUSY/RDY: modeled as high only while a conversion runs in the auto-sequence modes (SEL_OPMODE 1xxb); the datasheet keeps it high for a whole sequence (SEQ_START to completion/abort), during power-up calibration and address re-evaluation",
  "digital window comparator, hysteresis, pre-alert event counter, latched flags and the open-drain ALERT pin: stored only, ALERT never driven",
  "offset calibration, high-speed mode master codes (HS_MODE), I2C bus clear"
 ],
